  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "1. Weights and activations sit in GDDR6, 48 GB with ECC across the card.",
      "focus": ["gddr-left", "gddr-right"],
      "dot": "gddr-left",
      "explode": 0.6,
      "drill": null,
      "stage": "gddr"
    },
    {
      "text": "2. The 384-bit memory controller reads GDDR6 at up to 864 GB/s.",
      "focus": ["mc"],
      "dot": "mc",
      "stage": "memory-controller"
    },
    {
      "text": "3. Data lands in the 96 MB L2 cache — large enough to hold hot weights or a render's working set without going back to GDDR6.",
      "focus": ["l2"],
      "dot": "l2",
      "stage": "l2"
    },
    {
      "text": "4. Tiles move into each SM's 128 KB L1/shared memory.",
      "focus": ["sm-a"],
      "dot": "sm-a",
      "drill": "sm-detail",
      "stage": "shared-memory"
    },
    {
      "text": "5. One of 568 fourth-gen Tensor Cores multiplies the tile, e.g. in FP8 — doubled throughput if the weights are 2:4 structurally sparse.",
      "focus": ["tensor-core"],
      "dot": "tensor-core",
      "drill": "sm-detail",
      "stage": "tensor-core"
    },
    {
      "text": "6. In parallel, one of 142 third-gen RT Cores can walk the BVH and test ray intersections for rendering workloads sharing the same SM.",
      "focus": ["rt-core"],
      "dot": "rt-core",
      "drill": "sm-detail",
      "stage": "rt-core"
    },
    {
      "text": "7. Partial sums accumulate in the register file.",
      "focus": ["register-file"],
      "dot": "register-file",
      "drill": "sm-detail",
      "stage": "accumulate"
    },
    {
      "text": "8. Epilogue: the warp scheduler and CUDA cores apply bias, activation or shading, then quantize back down if needed.",
      "focus": ["warp-scheduler"],
      "dot": "warp-scheduler",
      "drill": "sm-detail",
      "stage": "epilogue"
    },
    {
      "text": "9. Results write back through L2 to GDDR6, or straight out: to the display engine's DisplayPort outputs for rendering, or to NVENC for streaming.",
      "focus": ["l2", "display-engine", "video-engine"],
      "dot": "l2",
      "drill": null,
      "stage": "writeback"
    },
    {
      "text": "10. With no NVLink, any multi-GPU traffic — or the host round-trip — goes out over PCIe Gen4 x16.",
      "focus": ["pcie"],
      "dot": "pcie",
      "drill": null,
      "stage": "pcie"
    }
  ],
